    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSituated in a quiet enclave within this popular residential development, just a short distance from Shankill Village, No. 56 is a superb three-bedroom semi-detached home extending to approximately 80 sq.m. \nBeautifully presented throughout, the property enjoys an enviable 38m long south-facing rear garden and has been thoughtfully designed with modern family living in mind.\nInternally, the accommodation is bright, spacious and welcoming. The entrance hallway features attractive wood flooring installed in 2021, recessed lighting and all new doors and windows throughout installed in 2026. To the left lies the elegant living room, which also benefits from wood flooring, recessed lighting, fitted shelving and a feature fireplace. Glass-panelled interconnecting doors lead to the open-plan kitchen/dining room, which spans the full width of the property. This superb family space incorporates wood flooring, a range of wall and floor units, an integrated oven and hob, subway-tiled splashback and recessed lighting, while French doors open directly to the rear garden.\nMeasuring approximately 38m in length, the private south-facing rear garden is undoubtedly one of the property's most impressive features. Immediately outside the kitchen/dining room is a decked area, installed in 2023, ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining. Beyond, the lawn is bordered by raised flowerbeds, while a further wild garden at the far end provides additional space and a natural retreat. Gated side access connects the garden to the front of the property.\nOn the first-floor level, there are three bedrooms, all with walnut wood flooring. A generous double to the front and a good sized single. To the rear there is a large double room with views to the garden and finally a family bathroom with modern suite and overhead electric shower. Attic access is provided via a Stira staircase on the landing.\nShankill retains a wonderful village atmosphere and vibrant sense of community, offering the perfect blend of coastal, country and suburban living thanks to its enviable location on the Dublin/Wicklow border. Residents enjoy an abundance of local amenities including shops, cafés, Lidl and Tesco Express supermarkets, childcare facilities and a tennis club. The nearby beach and Shanganagh Park, with its scenic walkways and playground, provide excellent recreational opportunities for everyday family life.\nThe area is well served by an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools, including St. Anne's National School, Rathmichael National School, Scoil Mhuire Primary School, Woodbrook College and Holy Child Killiney. \nShankill is renowned for its superb transport links, with regular DART and Dublin Bus services providing easy access to Dublin City Centre and beyond. The nearby N11, M11 and M50 road networks offer excellent connectivity, while the LUAS at Cherrywood is just a short distance away.\nEarly viewing of this most attractive family home is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nFront: - \nDriveway in tarmac with parking for 2 cars, lawn, hedge to left, gated side passage to right.\n\nHall - 1.60m x 4.96m\nAttractive wood flooring (2021), composite hall door along with all windows (2026), internal glass panelled doors, under stairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - 2.93m x 4.85m\nAttractive wood flooring (2021), feature fireplace, fitted shelving to left, glass panelled interconnecting doors to Kitchen/Diner.\n\nUSS - \n\n\nKitchen/Diner - 4.67m x 3.85m\nSpacious, width of the house, range of cabinetry (2023), subway tiled splashback, integrated oven and hob, French doors to garden.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.9m x 4.92m\nDouble room to rear, walnut wood flooring.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.65m x 3.72m\nDouble room to the front with walnut wood flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.90m x 2.70m\nSingle room to the front with walnut wood flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.68m x 2.30m\nModern, wash hand basin, W.C., bath with overhead electric shower.\n\nHot Press - \n\n\nLanding - \nCarpet stairs, hot press, Stira to attic.\n\nGarden: - \nDecking laid in 2021, central lawn, raised flower beds either side, beyond the gate garden extends a further 38m approx. and is a wild garden.\n\n"
      },
